                "ev-771567f1beb9-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The totality of the circumstances, including the packaged narcotics, established probable cause to arrest all occupants."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Srinivasan",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "771567f1beb98787beb477cf982ff7f967b0fdc9151f5e6eda5951915c40b989",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-771567f1beb9-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 22,
                "start": 22
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Srinivasan, when drugs packaged for distribution are readily discoverable by passengers, a reasonable officer may infer that each passenger is likely aware of the drugs."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Forster",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "771567f1beb98787beb477cf982ff7f967b0fdc9151f5e6eda5951915c40b989",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-771567f1beb9-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Forster, the driver can be imputed knowledge of the contents of the car and therefore may be arrested."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Maryland (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Forster",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "771567f1beb98787beb477cf982ff7f967b0fdc9151f5e6eda5951915c40b989",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-771567f1beb9-0002-0011"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 46,
                "start": 46
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Forster, possession requires not just knowledge, but also the intent to exercise dominion and control over the drug."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Forster",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "771567f1beb98787beb477cf982ff7f967b0fdc9151f5e6eda5951915c40b989",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-771567f1beb9-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 41,
                "start": 41
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Forster, because the drugs were concealed and not visible to the occupants, the situation is analogous to Di Re, where mere presence does not create probable cause."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Srinivasan",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "771567f1beb98787beb477cf982ff7f967b0fdc9151f5e6eda5951915c40b989",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-771567f1beb9-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 30,
                "start": 30
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Srinivasan, innocent persons may be arrested, and the probable cause standard accepts that possibility as a cost of effective law enforcement."
        }
      ],
